@title The Wintering
@bg northmire
@mood grief

narrate The winter after Sallow's Rest was the longest of Corin's life, and he spent it in a hut on the north edge of the Mire with a trapper called Halla who did not talk before noon.
@card halla
halla neutral "You're the one who got up."
corin neutral "Everyone keeps saying that."
halla dry "It's the only interesting thing about you."

narrate She taught him to set a snare, and to read a track, and to sit still for four hours in the cold without deciding anything.

choice
* "Ask her about the Coven"          => truth+1, lore:north_mire_coven
* "Say nothing. Watch the snow."     => conviction+1
* [Bonds 3] "Tell her about Marek."  => bonds+2, lore:marek_bakery
end

narrate He did not think about the bread that winter. That was the first sign, and he did not notice it.

@ach mod_wintering
@diary places the north Mire
